What about for those models that don't have OpenAI endpoints routes like Anthrophic's? They seem to not to work for whatever reason:

<img width="895" height="172" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/928e822a-9282-4b85-aa3f-f5db30c24f13" />

As for models that have an OpenAI endpoint such as Kimi-K2.5, configuring it as an /openai/v1 model works... until it doesn't and starts exposing the Tool Calls for some reason:

<img width="1089" height="108" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/40db99d4-d942-47c9-97aa-04680355a2cf" />

```json
  "provider": {
    "openai-compatible": {
        "options": {
            "baseURL": "https://RESOURCE_NAME.services.ai.azure.com/models",
            "apiKey": "REDACTED",
            "timeout": 300000
          },
        "models": {
            "Kimi-K2.5": {
                "name": "Kimi-K2.5",
                "limit": {
                  "context": 262144,
                  "output": 10000
                },
            }
        }
    }
```

I personally think that Azure is really not well integrated with OpenCode and must be worked on, or that the documentation is poor at best. My company uses Azure so it's the only thing we have available, and Claude Code (thru Azure Foundry) is costing us hundreds; [even Claude has proper documentation on configuring Azure Foundry](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/microsoft-foundry).

Variants are not respected in both TUI and desktop, even though they are configured in opencode.json:
```{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "openai": {
      "models": {
        "gpt-5.3-codex": {
          "variants": {
            "low": {
              "reasoningEffort": "low",
              "reasoningSummary": "auto",
              "textVerbosity": "medium",
              "disabled": false
            },
            "medium": {
              "reasoningEffort": "medium",
              "reasoningSummary": "auto",
              "textVerbosity": "medium",
              "disabled": false
            },
            "high": {
              "reasoningEffort": "high",
              "reasoningSummary": "auto",
              "textVerbosity": "medium",
              "disabled": false
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "agent": {
    "build": {
      "model": "openai/gpt-5.3-codex",
      "variant": "medium"
    },
    "plan": {
      "model": "openai/gpt-5.3-codex",
      "variant": "high"
    }
  }
}
```
When changing agents, the default variant is not used.

> What about for those models that don't have OpenAI endpoints routes like Anthrophic's? They seem to not to work for whatever reason:

@ktzug I just ended up setting two different custom providers: one for OpenAI-style endpoints and another one for Anthropic's. You can use the `@ai-sdk/anthropic` package:


```json
  "provider": {
    "azure-anthropic": {
      "name": "Azure Foundry Anthropic",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/anthropic",
      "api": "https://RESOURCE_NAME.services.ai.azure.com/anthropic/v1",
      "models": {
        "claude-sonnet-4-6": {
          "id": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
          "name": "Claude Sonnet 4.6",
          "tool_call": true,
          "attachment": true,
          "reasoning": true,
          "temperature": true
        }
      }
    }
  }
```

However I gotta agree documentation is severely lacking.
